{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Joseph said, etc. — 'Come near, I pray you,' etc.</b> The reason for the drawing near is that since he wished to tell them the matter of recognition, he did not wish to tell them except in a whisper. Therefore he said ״גְּשׁוּ״, and after they drew near he said to them, etc., ״אֲשֶׁר מְכַרְתֶּם אוֹתִי״ — and even though he had said ״הוֹצִיאוּ כָל אִישׁ״, etc., and no man remained there, nevertheless he was cautious of ears to the wall and spoke into their ears." "<b>I am Joseph your brother, etc.</b> The reason he repeated a second time <b>I am Joseph</b>, is that since he saw they did not answer him, he was concerned about two things: the first, that they were terrified of him and could not reply out of the shame of a thief when he is found; and the second, that they did not believe him that he was Joseph. Therefore he said, corresponding to the aspect of fear — that you are afraid and dismayed, do not be concerned about anything, for I am Joseph your brother, meaning: I conduct myself toward you with the trait of brotherhood as though that matter had never been. He also drew support to say <b>your brother whom you sold</b>, to say that even at the time of the sale, the eye of brotherhood did not dim within me. And corresponding to the aspect of verifying the matter — that he is Joseph — he told them something through which they would verify with an unmistakable sign that it is indeed he, in saying <b>whom you sold me to Egypt</b>, and this thing no man knew, not even a prophet (Yalkut Shimoni 142), unless you say it is an absolute certainty that this is Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:47.777468923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}